If `_impartial(self.call)` is a class, then `inspect.isgeneratorfunction(_impartial(self.call))` is False.
But `getattr(_impartial(self.call), "__call__", None)` will be the `__call__` method of the class.

So if `inspect.isclass(_impartial(self.call))`, we should probably skip the `dunder_call` checks.

